  "evidence": "Full continuous paved circuit independently digitized from the pinned licensed native satellite mosaic using 97 manual image-centre controls. No original OSM trace coordinates or source-guided alignment-proposal coordinates are used to construct these final vertices. The operator identifies this facility as Circuito Paladino. The image identifies the continuous paved loop; configuration and direction remain draft. The manual image controls are resampled at 3 m arc intervals, filtered by a periodic 3 m Gaussian and simplified within 0.15 m of that fitted curve. These are numerical processing tolerances, not surveyed accuracy or independent observations. No nominal course length or road width is fitted. Imagery acquisition date and georeferencing error are unknown; raw imagery is not redistributed."
